---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="tokiOS — Agent Systems Infrastructure"
  description="tokiOS provides the systems layer that gives AI agents durable identity, governed context, persistent memory, authority, coordination, isolation, recovery, and concurrent execution."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="shell">
      <p class="eyebrow">Agent systems infrastructure</p>

      <h1>Give AI agents the system capabilities they do not inherit from the model.</h1>

      <p class="hero-copy">
        Foundation models provide inference. tokiOS provides the systems layer
        that gives AI agents durable identity, governed context, persistent
        memory, authority, capabilities, coordination, isolation, recovery, and
        concurrent execution across distributed infrastructure.
      </p>

      <div class="actions">
        <a class="button primary" href="/research/">Explore the research</a>
        <a
          class="button"
          href="/research/tokimind/governed-persistent-memory-300h/"
        >
          Read the tokiMind study
        </a>
      </div>

      <div class="proof-strip" aria-label="Published research evidence">
        <div class="proof-item">
          <strong>300 hours</strong>
          <span>Longitudinal evaluation</span>
        </div>

        <div class="proof-item">
          <strong>1,932 runs</strong>
          <span>Durable scheduled executions</span>
        </div>

        <div class="proof-item">
          <strong>350 / 350</strong>
          <span>tokiMind scored recall</span>
        </div>

        <div class="proof-item">
          <strong>Published V1</strong>
          <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23175185">
            10.5281/zenodo.23175185
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell">
      <p class="eyebrow">Operating layer</p>
      <h2>Beyond runtimes and orchestration.</h2>

      <p class="lead definition">
        Frameworks help build agents. Harnesses help test and inspect them.
        Runtimes execute model loops. Orchestrators coordinate workflows. tokiOS
        provides the broader systems layer that gives multiple AI agents durable
        identity, governed context, persistent memory, authority, coordination,
        isolation, recovery, and concurrent operation.
      </p>

      <div class="category-grid">
        <article class="category-card">
          <span>Framework</span>
          <p>Helps developers build an agent.</p>
        </article>

        <article class="category-card">
          <span>Harness</span>
          <p>Helps developers test, inspect, simulate, debug, and control agents.</p>
        </article>

        <article class="category-card">
          <span>Runtime / orchestrator</span>
          <p>Executes agents and coordinates units of work.</p>
        </article>

        <article class="category-card category-card-emphasis">
          <span>tokiOS operating layer</span>
          <p>
            Gives multiple AI agents durable identity, governed context,
            persistent memory, authority, coordination, isolation, recovery,
            and concurrent execution across distributed infrastructure.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section system-section">
    <div class="shell">
      <p class="eyebrow">System layers</p>
      <h2>Identity. Context. Memory. Authority. Durable execution.</h2>

      <p class="lead">
        tokiOS provides these operating capabilities through coordinated system
        layers. VICA governs identity, behavior, voice, authority, and context
        engineering; tokiMind governs persistent memory; and tokiLab provides
        the experimental infrastructure used to evaluate the system.
      </p>

      <div class="grid">
        <article class="card">
          <h3>VICA</h3>
          <p>
            Voice Identity Context Acceptance. VICA is tokiOS context
            engineering: separate governed Mindset and Context Envelopes define
            who an agent is, how it reasons and communicates, which voice and
            behavioral posture it uses, what authority binds it, and what
            knowledge and state may enter an invocation.
          </p>
        </article>

        <a
          class="card card-link"
          href="/research/tokimind/governed-persistent-memory-300h/"
        >
          <h3>tokiMind</h3>
          <p>
            The governed persistent-memory system evaluated in our published
            research and the subject of a pending U.S. patent application.
            tokiMind governs provenance, trust, contradiction, supersession,
            freshness, revocation, tenant isolation, and scoped retrieval so
            agents do not own or serve memory unchecked.
          </p>
          <span class="card-cta">View published research →</span>
        </a>

        <article class="card">
          <h3>tokiLab</h3>
          <p>
            Experimental infrastructure for frozen, durable, longitudinal
            evaluation of agent behavior and state-management systems.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
